&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About Vercel:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Vercel is the agentic infrastructure company, freeing people and agents to ship what&#39;s next. For more than a decade we&#39;ve helped builders move from idea to production with speed, security, and exceptional developer experience.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Now we&#39;re scaling our products for both agents and people to ship and run software, built in the open and trusted by OpenAI, PayPal, Ramp, Supreme, and millions of developers worldwide.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the Role:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI Gateway gives developers one place to connect applications and agents to hundreds of models with one API key. It handles provider routing and fallbacks, unifies billing and observability, and lets teams manage spend and security controls across production AI workloads.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Designing this well is a systems problem. A developer should be able to choose the right model, make and verify a first request, diagnose a failed request, and configure routing, budgets, credentials, and security controls without losing sight of the application they are trying to build. The right interface might be in the dashboard, on the public model catalog, in the CLI, in an API response, or in code.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be the Design Engineer for AI Gateway, owning product design and frontend implementation across those surfaces. You will work with customers, a Product Manager, and engineers to understand the problem, explore solutions, build the production experience, ship it, and learn from what happens after launch.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI Gateway is live, the model ecosystem changes every week, and the team can move from an observed problem to production quickly. This is a rare chance to use your product judgment, design craft, and code to shape a developer product and ship the experience yourself.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be the design owner embedded with a Product Manager and a dedicated engineering team. You will also have the Product Design team around you for critique, collaboration, and support. AI Gateway will be your main product area, with room to pursue design-led improvements across Vercel. You will report to the Design Team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re based within a pre-determined commuting distance of one of our offices (SF, NY, London, or Berlin), the role includes in-office anchor days on Monday, Tuesday, and Friday. If you&#39;re located beyond that distance, the role is fully remote. For location-specific details, please connect with our recruiting team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You Will Do:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own product design and frontend implementation for meaningful parts of the journey from discovering a model to making a first successful request and operating AI in production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and build production experiences across the website, dashboard, CLI, and APIs, choosing the right medium for each problem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make models, providers, credentials, routing, budgets, logs, performance, privacy, and governance understandable, then create patterns that extend across new providers, modalities, and workloads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Talk directly with customers and use product data to understand problems, define success, make tradeoffs, and improve what ships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own quality after launch, including visual and interaction craft, accessibility, performance, resilience, instrumentation, and edge cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use coding agents to explore and implement ideas quickly, while testing, debugging, and taking responsibility for what ships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About You:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Your work shows what you personally identified, designed, built, shipped, and learned after launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You build production-quality web applications with React and TypeScript and can contribute confidently in a large, existing codebase.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You bring strong visual and interaction craft and have made technical or data-rich products understandable without removing the control advanced users need.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can move between graphical interfaces, CLI workflows, API behavior, and implementation details, treating accessibility, performance, failure recovery, and instrumentation as part of the design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You use customer research and product data to make decisions, communicate your reasoning clearly, challenge ideas constructively, and change direction when the evidence changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You use coding agents in your daily work, but you can explain, test, debug, and take responsibility for the code they help produce.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;There is no required path into this role. You may come from product design, frontend engineering, creative development, or a career that does not fit a standard title. We care about the quality of what you have shipped and the judgment behind it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Bonus If You:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience with developer tools, infrastructure products, model marketplaces, or observability experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have worked with AI models, providers, inference platforms, guardrails, or AI application tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience with APIs, command-line tools, structured product content, or agent-facing interfaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have built an application or agent with Vercel’s AI SDK or AI Gateway.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;See the work:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://vercel.com/ai-gateway&quot;&gt;AI Gateway&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://vercel.com/docs/ai-gateway&quot;&gt;AI Gateway documentation&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://vercel.com/ai-gateway/models&quot;&gt;Browse AI models&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://vercel.com/ai-gateway/leaderboards/models&quot;&gt;AI model leaderboards&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://vercel.com/blog/design-engineering-at-vercel&quot;&gt;Design Engineering at Vercel&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Compensation &amp;amp; Benefits:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Competitive compensation package, including equity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Inclusive Healthcare Package.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Learn and Grow - we provide mentorship and send you to events that help you build your network and skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Flexible Time Off.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;We will provide you the gear you need to do your role, and a WFH budget for you to outfit your space as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;The San Francisco, CA base pay range for this role is $208,000 - $312,000. Actual salary will be based on job-related skills, experience, and location. Compensation outside of San Francisco may be adjusted based on employee location. The total compensation package may include benefits, equity-based compensation, and eligibility for a company bonus or variable pay program depending on the role. Your recruiter can share more details during the hiring process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;te-floating-button-container&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Disclosures:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy: &lt;/strong&gt;Please review our &lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://vercel.com/legal/job-applicant-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;Job Applicant Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; for more information on how we handle your data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Vercel is committed to fostering and empowering an inclusive community within our organization. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, gender expression or identity, sexual orientation, national origin, citizenship, age, marital status, veteran status, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Vercel encourages everyone to apply for our available positions, even if they don&#39;t necessarily check every box on the job description.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About Vercel:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Vercel is the agentic infrastructure company, freeing people and agents to ship what&#39;s next. For more than a decade we&#39;ve helped builders move from idea to production with speed, security, and exceptional developer experience.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Now we&#39;re scaling our products for both agents and people to ship and run software, built in the open and trusted by OpenAI, PayPal, Ramp, Supreme, and millions of developers worldwide.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the Role:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll lead the team responsible for Vercel’s CDN, proxy, and edge caching systems—the core infrastructure that powers performance, reliability, and cost efficiency for every customer request at Vercel. Your mandate is twofold:&amp;nbsp;Operate critical systems exceptionally (latency, reliability, COGS), and align the team to product and business goals, translating strategy into a clear roadmap&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will set direction, grow people, and create the conditions for high trust, high autonomy, and high output—balancing technical depth with strong people leadership.&amp;nbsp;This is a manager role, not a principal IC role. You’ll code when it’s the highest leverage (e.g., prototypes/unblocking), but your default is delegation, coaching, and alignment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About You:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years building and operating large-scale distributed systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years managing engineers (managing managers is a plus)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success leading CDN/proxy/caching/edge or similar high-throughput, low-latency infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to translate business goals into technical strategy and drive cross-org alignment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record establishing trust, psychological safety, and clear expectations; skilled at timely, candid feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong facilitator in technical conflict—you listen, synthesize, decide, and bring the team with you&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competence across HTTP, TLS, caching strategies, load shedding, capacity planning, observability, and cost optimization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Bonus If You:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience with&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;Go, Lua, or Node at the edge; running high-signal hiring pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborating with product/PMM on customer-facing narratives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Benefits &amp;amp; Compensation:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Competitive compensation package, including equity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Inclusive Healthcare Package.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Learn and Grow - we provide mentorship and send you to events that help you build your network and skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Flexible Time Off.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;We will provide you the gear you need to do your role, and a WFH budget for you to outfit your space as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;The San Francisco, CA base pay range for this role is $196,000.00 - $336,000.00. Actual salary will be based on job-related skills, experience, and location. Compensation outside of San Francisco may be adjusted based on employee location. The total compensation package may include benefits, equity-based compensation, and eligibility for a company bonus or variable pay program depending on the role. Your recruiter can share more details during the hiring process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;te-floating-button-container&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Disclosures:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy: &lt;/strong&gt;Please review our &lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://vercel.com/legal/job-applicant-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;Job Applicant Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; for more information on how we handle your data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Vercel is committed to fostering and empowering an inclusive community within our organization. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, gender expression or identity, sexual orientation, national origin, citizenship, age, marital status, veteran status, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Vercel encourages everyone to apply for our available positions, even if they don&#39;t necessarily check every box on the job description.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About Vercel:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Vercel is the agentic infrastructure company, freeing people and agents to ship what&#39;s next. For more than a decade we&#39;ve helped builders move from idea to production with speed, security, and exceptional developer experience.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Now we&#39;re scaling our products for both agents and people to ship and run software, built in the open and trusted by OpenAI, PayPal, Ramp, Supreme, and millions of developers worldwide.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Vercel:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Vercel&#39;s Frontend Cloud provides the developer experience and infrastructure to build, scale, and secure faster, more personalized web applications. Customers like Under Armour, Nintendo, The Washington Post, Porsche, and Zapier rely on Vercel to create dynamic, seamless user experiences on the web.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to empower the world to deliver the best digital products. That mission extends to building a supportive, innovative workplace where you can do the best work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Engineering Manager on the Dashboard team, you will lead a team of engineers responsible for the primary interface developers use to build, deploy, and manage applications on Vercel. The Dashboard is where customers experience the platform every day, from onboarding new projects to managing deployments, observability, billing, security, AI, and team collaboration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll partner closely with Product, Design, Data, and other engineering teams to deliver intuitive, high-quality product experiences while helping shape the long-term architecture of one of Vercel&#39;s most important customer-facing surfaces. This role requires balancing technical leadership, product thinking, and strong people management to help the team ship quickly without compromising quality.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and grow a high-performing team of engineers through hiring, coaching, mentorship, and thoughtful career development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a culture of ownership, collaboration, and high engineering standards while creating an environment where engineers can do their best work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Product, Design, and other engineering teams to define roadmap priorities and execute against ambitious product goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help the team make sound technical decisions around frontend architecture, performance, reliability, and developer experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Occasionally review and contribute code to stay close to the technology and unblock the team when needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive operational excellence through strong engineering processes, incident management, and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balance short-term product delivery with long-term investments in technical quality and platform scalability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion a customer-first mindset, ensuring the Dashboard remains fast, intuitive, and delightful for developers of all sizes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience leading and growing high-performing engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have built and operated large-scale customer-facing web applications or developer products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a strong product engineering mindset and enjoy working closely with product managers and designers to deliver polished user experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience building modern web applications using technologies such as React, Next.js, TypeScript, and the broader JavaScript ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You understand frontend architecture, performance optimization, accessibility, and design systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You communicate clearly across technical and non-technical audiences and can build alignment across teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You thrive in fast-moving environments and are comfortable making decisions with incomplete information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You care deeply about creating an inclusive team culture where engineers can grow and have meaningful impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits &amp;amp; Compensation:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive compensation package and stock options.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive, inclusive healthcare package.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunities for mentorship and professional growth, including attendance at industry events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible Time Off with a recommended minimum of four weeks per year, plus paid holidays.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remote-friendly culture with teammates across multiple time zones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Dedicated equipment and work-from-home budget to help you create an effective workspace.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The San Francisco, CA base pay range for this role is $226,000-$325,000. Actual salary will be based on job-related skills, experience, and location. Compensation outside of San Francisco may be adjusted based on employee location. The total compensation package may include benefits, equity-based compensation, and eligibility for a company bonus or variable pay program depending on the role. Your recruiter can share more details during the hiring process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Disclosures:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy: &lt;/strong&gt;Please review our &lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://vercel.com/legal/job-applicant-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;Job Applicant Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; for more information on how we handle your data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Vercel is committed to fostering and empowering an inclusive community within our organization. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, gender expression or identity, sexual orientation, national origin, citizenship, age, marital status, veteran status, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Vercel encourages everyone to apply for our available positions, even if they don&#39;t necessarily check every box on the job description.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About Vercel:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Vercel is the agentic infrastructure company, freeing people and agents to ship what&#39;s next. For more than a decade we&#39;ve helped builders move from idea to production with speed, security, and exceptional developer experience.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Now we&#39;re scaling our products for both agents and people to ship and run software, built in the open and trusted by OpenAI, PayPal, Ramp, Supreme, and millions of developers worldwide.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Next.js team builds the open source framework that powers millions of applications and shapes how developers build for the web. Our work sits at the intersection of React, framework architecture, developer experience, infrastructure, performance, and production reliability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an Engineering Team Lead to help build and lead a team working on Next.js. This is a hands-on player/coach role for an experienced engineer who wants to remain close to the code while helping a small team do its best work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be an engineer first and a manager second. You will contribute directly to the framework, lead major technical initiatives, review code, debug complex production issues, and help make architectural decisions. You will also support the engineers around you through clear direction, thoughtful feedback, and practical coaching.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is not a traditional people management role. You will spend the majority of your time on technical leadership and engineering execution. You should be comfortable owning difficult parts of the codebase while creating enough context and clarity for others to move quickly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work closely with Product, Design, and engineers across Vercel to guide the evolution of Next.js across rendering, caching, routing, build systems, and developer tooling.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build and ship Next.js:&lt;/strong&gt; Write production code, review pull requests, debug difficult issues, and contribute directly to the framework and its supporting systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead major technical initiatives:&lt;/strong&gt; Take ownership of complex projects from initial exploration through architecture, implementation, rollout, and production follow-through.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Set technical direction:&lt;/strong&gt; Make sound architectural decisions across rendering, caching, routing, build systems, runtime behavior, and developer tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stay close to real problems:&lt;/strong&gt; Investigate performance regressions, production failures, and developer pain points. Turn what you learn into practical improvements to the framework.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Raise the engineering bar:&lt;/strong&gt; Establish strong patterns for code quality, testing, performance, reliability, observability, and incremental delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Coach through the work:&lt;/strong&gt; Help engineers grow through pairing, design reviews, code reviews, technical feedback, and shared ownership of challenging problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Provide focused people leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Set clear expectations, give candid feedback, support career development, and help maintain a high-trust and accountable team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Improve team execution:&lt;/strong&gt; Create lightweight planning and decision-making practices that clarify ownership, reduce unnecessary coordination, and help the team ship consistently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner across Vercel:&lt;/strong&gt; Work with Product, Design, Infrastructure, Developer Experience, and other engineering teams so framework changes integrate cleanly across the Vercel platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Champion open source:&lt;/strong&gt; Work in public, engage thoughtfully with contributors, and balance community needs with the team’s product and technical priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Help grow the team:&lt;/strong&gt; Participate in recruiting, assess technical talent, and help new engineers become productive in a complex codebase.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 8+ years of software engineering experience and remain highly effective as a hands-on engineer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have led engineers or small technical teams, whether as a team lead, tech lead, staff engineer, engineering manager, or founder.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have recent experience writing, reviewing, and shipping production code. You are not looking to step away from engineering execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have strong technical judgment across React, framework architecture, or the systems behind a large-scale open source project, including rendering, caching, routing, build tooling, and runtime behavior.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can take a complex technical problem, form a clear point of view, write the critical code, and bring other engineers along with you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You know when to lead from the front and when to create space for someone else to take ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience building products or infrastructure for developers and understand the quality, performance, stability, and usability standards this audience expects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You think in systems and can guide a team toward clean abstractions, consistent framework patterns, and technical decisions that hold up at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable working through ambiguity and solving problems from first principles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You balance speed and quality. You favor incremental delivery and real-world feedback while recognizing when foundational infrastructure requires deeper investment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You communicate clearly in writing, facilitate productive technical debate, and make decisions when a path forward is needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You use AI tools in your own workflow and have informed opinions about how agentic products should work for developers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience maintaining or contributing to a major open source project, particularly in the React or Next.js ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with compilers, bundlers, caching, rendering systems, or distributed infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading a small, senior engineering team while continuing to make substantial individual contributions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience forming a team or technical direction from zero to one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with the Next.js codebase, though this is not required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Compensation &amp;amp; Benefits:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive compensation package, including equity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inclusive healthcare package.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learning and growth support, including mentorship and opportunities to attend events that build your network and skills.&lt;/li&gt;
